############ ACCESS SWITCHES (2960) - optional hostname only ############
enable
configure terminal
hostname SW-CSE        (use SW-ECE / SW-EEE / SW-Admin on the others)
end
write memory
 
STEP 4 - END DEVICES (PCs)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
 PC > Desktop > IP Configuration > select DHCP.
 Expected first leases:
   CSE-PC1 192.168.10.6    CSE-PC2 192.168.10.7
   ECE-PC1 192.168.10.70   ECE-PC2 192.168.10.71
   EEE-PC1 192.168.10.134  EEE-PC2 192.168.10.135
   Admin-PC1 192.168.10.166  Admin-PC2 192.168.10.167
 
 (If DHCP is not wanted, set static IPs from the same pools with the
  gateway of that department and the mask from the tables.)
 
STEP 5 - VERIFICATION
---------------------------------------------------------------------
 On CORE-L3:
   show ip route
   show ip interface brief
 On any router:
   show ip interface brief
   show ip dhcp binding
   show running-config
 On PCs (Desktop > Command Prompt):
   ipconfig
   ping 192.168.10.1                 (own gateway, from CSE-PC1)
   ping 192.168.10.7                 (same department)
   ping 192.168.10.70                (CSE -> ECE)
   ping 192.168.10.134               (CSE -> EEE)
   ping 192.168.10.166               (CSE -> Admin)
   tracert 192.168.10.166            (expect hops .1, .193, .206, .166)
 
 Note: first ping may show 1 timeout while ARP resolves; repeat it.
 Take screenshots of topology, show ip route, ipconfig and pings
 for the report.
